-- title:
--   Uniqueness of Gauss-type valuations on the j-line of X_H(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, write $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lie in $A$. Assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, and that every element of $A$ differs from some element of $A_0$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $N \geq 1$ with $q \nmid N$, let $H \leq (\mathbb Z/N)^\times$, and let $K''$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$ obtained by adjoining to $k_0$ the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb Q \to k_0$ of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField N H`, with $K''$ an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $A_0 \to k_0 \to K''$. Let $j'' \in K''$ be the element whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of `jq`, the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$. Then any two valuation subrings $V, V'$ of $K''$ that each contain the image of $A_0$, send $\pi_0$ to a non-unit, and satisfy $P(j'') \in V$ and $P(j'')^{-1} \in V$ for every polynomial $P$ over $A_0$ not divisible by $\pi_0$, are equal.
--
--   This is the uniqueness assertion for the Gauss-type valuation of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H(N)$ over a discretely valued base at a residue characteristic prime to the level; the Gauss-type clause fixes the valuation on $k_0(j'')$ and, since the residue degree of the Gauss prolongation is full when $q \nmid N$ (Igusa's theorem), the prolongation is determined. It is used in the analysis of minimal primes over $(\pi_0)$ in the chart algebras attached to $X_H(N)$.
